config MQTT_INIT_PIGEON_ID
  string "Pigeon id this device connects to the broker as"
  default ""
  help
    The pigeon's own 64-character hex id, passed to pigeon_init() as
    pigeon_config.device_id -- which on the MQTT connector is the CONNECT
    client id and username, and (on a PSK build) the handshake identity as
    well. The broker refuses anything else and refuses a session whose
    three copies of it disagree, so this is a real credential-shaped value:
    it belongs in the git-ignored prj.local.conf next to the endpoint and
    the PSK secret, never in tracked source.

    The empty default fails loudly at pigeon_mqtt_start() rather than
    silently connecting as nobody.

menu "Zephyr Kernel"
source "Kconfig.zephyr"
endmenu
